      "description": "Skill then evidence; mono for code-read proof, muted italic for self-added.",
      "html": "<ul class=\"ds-proof\"><li><span class=\"ds-skill\">React</span><span class=\"ds-ev\">4 original repos, 6 days ago</span></li><li><span class=\"ds-skill\">Python</span><span class=\"ds-ev\">2 original repos, 1 month ago</span></li><li><span class=\"ds-skill ds-self\">UI design</span><span class=\"ds-ev ds-self-ev\">Self-added, Figma portfolio</span></li></ul>",
      "css": ":host{--navy:#14213d;--navy-deep:#0e1830;--cream:#f4ede0;--coral:#ff6b5b;--canvas:#f4ede0;--paper:#fbf8f2;--sunken:#ebe3d4;--ink:#14213d;--ink-soft:#2e3a55;--muted:#5b6478;--line:#ded4c2;--line-strong:#c9bda8;--action:#ff6b5b;--action-hover:#ff8577;--action-ink:#14213d;--accent:#b8392a;--accent-soft:#fbe2dc;--danger:#a3261b;--danger-soft:#f8ddd8} .ds-proof{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;font-family:Geist,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:0.8125rem;line-height:1.25rem} .ds-proof li{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:6px} .ds-skill{width:96px;font-weight:500;color:var(--ink)} .ds-ev{font-family:\"Geist Mono\",ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--ink-soft)} .ds-self{color:var(--muted)} .ds-self-ev{font-family:inherit;font-style:italic;color:var(--muted)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Night Field with Commit Cells",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "night-field",
      "description": "Navy gradient, one coral bloom, commit-graph cells lit coral by activity.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-night\"><div class=\"ds-strip\"><i></i><i class=\"l\" style=\"opacity:.4\"></i><i></i><i class=\"l\" style=\"opacity:.7\"></i><i class=\"l g\" style=\"opacity:1\"></i><i class=\"l\" style=\"opacity:.55\"></i><i></i><i class=\"l g\" style=\"opacity:.9\"></i></div><p class=\"ds-night-h\">Proof you can see at night.</p></div>",
      "css": ".ds-night{padding:32px;border-radius:12px;color:#f4ede0;font-family:\"Bricolage Grotesque\",Geist,sans-serif;background:radial-gradient(55% 65% at 80% 92%,rgb(255 107 91/.5),transparent 62%),radial-gradient(35% 45% at 64% 70%,rgb(255 107 91/.14),transparent 70%),linear-gradient(180deg,#14213d 0%,#0e1830 100%)} .ds-strip{display:flex;gap:4px} .ds-strip i{width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:3px;background:rgb(244 237 224/.07)} .ds-strip i.l{background:#ff6b5b} .ds-strip i.g{box-shadow:0 0 14px 1px rgb(255 107 91/.4)} .ds-night-h{margin:16px 0 0;font-size:2rem;line-height:2.5rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.02em}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Build Night",
    "overview": "Sandbox is a campus after hours: a navy field where real activity glows. The public site lives at night (navy deepening to navy-deep, one coral light source, a faint commit-graph grid of rounded squares with a few cells lit), and the signed-in app lives in the calm of day (cream ground, navy ink, coral reserved for the action). Dark mode carries the night values into the app. The two scopes are one token set, swapped by `.theme-night` or `prefers-color-scheme: dark`, so every component works in both without its own variant.\n\nThe system is flat and ruled. Depth comes from tone (paper over cream, sunken fills) and from 1px lines, never from elevation shadows. On the night field, panels become frosted glass: translucent cream at low alpha with a cream hairline and a backdrop blur. Proof is the product, so evidence read from code is set in Geist Mono and everything self-claimed is visibly quieter.\n\nDensity is generous on the public site (80 to 112px section rhythm, display type up to 72px) and moderate in the app (24px panel padding, a single heading per page). Motion is a confident deceleration that tells the matching story once, then stops.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Founder-pinned palette: Navy, Cream, Coral; nothing else carries hue except the danger pair.",
      "Two scopes, one token set: day (cream) for the app, night (navy field) for the public site, header, footer, sign-in and dark mode.",
      "Coral is fill, glow and action; it never sets text on cream.",
      "Flat surfaces separated by 1px rules; the only box-shadow is a lit commit cell's glow.",
      "Mono type means \"read from code\"; italic muted means \"self-added\"."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Coral Never Writes On Cream Rule",
        "body": "Coral on cream measures 2.4:1. Coral may fill, glow or mark, but any coral-family text on a cream or paper ground uses Deep Coral (4.9:1).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Light Source Rule",
        "body": "Each night section has exactly one coral bloom, repositioned per section (lower right in the hero, lower left in proof, low centre at the close) so it never reads as a stamp.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Token-Only Rule",
        "body": "Components use the semantic utilities (canvas, paper, sunken, ink, muted, line, action, accent), never raw hex, so the day and night scopes swap cleanly.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Means Proof Rule",
        "body": "Geist Mono appears only on evidence read from code (repo names, proof lines, the match score). Self-added skills are muted italic Geist, never mono.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence-Case Label Rule",
        "body": "Panel labels (\"Your idea\", \"Repositories read\") are muted caption in sentence case. No uppercase tracked labels.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Lift Rule",
        "body": "Panels, menus, buttons and inputs carry no box-shadow. A dropdown separates by paper fill and a 1px line; glass separates by blur.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do set navy text on coral (5.7:1) and navy on cream (13.7:1); use Deep Coral (#B8392A, 4.9:1) for any coral-family text on cream.",
      "Do wrap public hero, header, footer, sign-in and night sections in the night scope, and let dark mode reuse the same values.",
      "Do separate sections with a 1px rule or a switch to the night field, and separate panel rows with 1px lines.",
      "Do set evidence read from code in Geist Mono and label everything illustrative as illustrative.",
      "Do reserve the message line under every field so errors never shift the layout.",
      "Do give every animation a reduced-motion path that keeps state change visible."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't set coral text on cream or paper (2.4:1).",
      "Don't add elevation shadows to panels, menus or buttons; the coral glow on lit cells is the only shadow.",
      "Don't add hues beyond navy, cream, coral and the danger pair.",
      "Don't place more than one coral light source in a night section, or the same bloom position in consecutive sections.",
      "Don't use mono for self-claimed skills or for decoration.",
      "Don't use uppercase tracked labels above headings; panel labels stay sentence-case captions."
    ]
  }
}
